    "name": "RC Thunderdome",
    "text": "2\nRC Thunderdome\nInstructions\n\nFor each passage*, write out an answer to each of the following:\n\nWhat's the Main Point?\n\nWhat's the tone of the passage?\n\nWho is the author?\n\nWho is the audience?\n\nWho are the players in the passage and what do they believe?\n\nStrengthen the author's opinion\n\nIf the passage feels neutral, write a confirming piece of evidence for the information the author is presenting.\n\nWeaken the author's opinion\n\nIf the passage feels neutral, write a disconfirming piece of evidence for the information the author is presenting.\n\nThree Inferences from the passage\n\nThree things the author is likely to believe\n\nParallel one piece of the passage\n\nPick an example, one line of reasoning, or a given person's point of view.\n\nOutline the structure of the passage\n\nYou can use paragraphs as an organizing structure, but you can also delineate on a more fine-grained level, if desired.\n\nSub out three words in the passage and replace them with a new word/phrase that means the same thing.\n\nPick three sentences out of the passage and identify their function\n\nIdentify a principle underlying the passage as a whole or an argument within the passage\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
