ed\">*</span>, write out an answer to each of the following:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>What's the Main Point?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What's the tone of the passage?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Who is the author?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Who is the audience?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Who are the players in the passage and what do they believe?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Strengthen the author's opinion</p>\n<ol>\n<li>If the passage feels neutral, write a confirming piece of evidence for the information the author is presenting.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Weaken the author's opinion</p>\n<ol>\n<li>If the passage feels neutral, write a disconfirming piece of evidence for the information the author is presenting.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Three Inferences from the passage</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Three things the author is likely to believe</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Parallel one piece of the&nbsp;passage</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Pick an example, one line of reasoning, or a given person's point of view.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Outline the structure of the passage</p>\n<ol>\n<li>You can use paragraphs as an organizing structure, but you can also delineate on a more fine-grained level, if desired.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Sub out three words in the passage and replace them with a new word/phrase that means the same thing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Pick three sentences out of the passage and identify their function</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Identify a principle underlying the passage as a whole or an argument within the passage</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"pt-2\"><a href=\"/workouts-and-routines/workouts/rc-thunderdome\"><button class=\"\n    inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-full\n    font-extrabold uppercase lh-outline\n    [transition:background-color_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),border-color_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),box-shadow_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),translate_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1)]\n    disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\n  