    "name": "Write In",
    "text": "3\nWrite In\nInstructions\n\nNOTE: The Write In replaces the Mission step of the Full LR Process.\n\nRead and translate the stimulus in chunks*. \n\nQuip each chunk of the stimulus after you translate.\n\nContinue until the end of the stimulus.\n\nMark the conclusion.\n\nImmediately proceed to the CLIR after your final quip of the stimulus (or the final quip is the CLIR).\n\nRead the question stem, identify the question type and whether the question is Powerful-Provable.\n\nWrite in a correct answer to the question.\n\nMake the Write In answer sound like a real answer choice, not a messy note.\n\nOn every individual answer choice:\n\nRead, translate, and quip the answer choice.\n\nInvestigate whether this answer choice meets the question type's Back Up Plan.\n\nIf you think this answer meets the Back-Up Plan question, highlight the first word of the answer.\n\nIf you are not sure whether this answer meets the Back-Up Plan question, leave it open.\n\nIf you know this answer doesn't meet the Back-Up Plan question, cross it out.\n\nChoose amongst the open and highlighted answer choices.\n\nHyperskip, if needed.\n\nAim to hyperskip 5-7 questions per section.\n\nUse any remaining time to return to your hyperskips.\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
